{title: Draw Me Nearer}
{key: D}
{x_theme: altar, cross, faith-trust, grace-mercy, joy, prayer, worship}
{x_source: chrd:draw_me_nearer.chrd}

{comment: Chorus}
Draw me nearer, [G]nearer blessed [D]Lord,
To the [G]cross where Thou hast [A]died;
Draw me [D]nearer, [Gbm]nearer, [G]nearer blessed [Em]Lord,
To Thy [D]precious, [A]bleeding [D]side.

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]I am [A]Thine, O Lord, I have [D]heard Thy voice,
And it [G]told Thy love to [D]me;
But I [A]long to rise in the [D]arms of faith
And be [G]closer [A]drawn to [D]Thee.

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]Conse[A]crate me now to Thy [D]service, Lord,
By the [G]pow'r of grace di[D]vine;
Let my [A]soul look up with a [D]steadfast hope,
And my [G]will be [A]lost in [D]Thine.

{comment: Verse 3}
[D]Oh, the [A]pure delight of a [D]single hour
That be[G]fore Thy throne I [D]spend,
When I [A]kneel in prayer, and with [D]Thee, my God
I com[G]mune as [A]friend with [D]friend!

{comment: Verse 4}
[D]There are [A]depths of love that I [D]cannot know
Till I [G]cross the narrow [D]sea;
There are [A]heights of joy that I [D]may not reach
Till I [G]rest in [A]peace with [D]Thee.
